{
  "id": "value_engineering",
  "title": "Value Engineering",
  "description": "Improved value by enhanced function.",
  "type": "calculator",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "# Value Engineering\n\nThe definition of value\n\n**V = F / C**\n\nwhere\n- **V** = value\n- **F** = function\n- **C** = cost\n\nis the key to Value Engineering. Improving the function, reducing the cost, or both - will increase the value."
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "function",
          "label": "Function (F)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 100
        },
        {
          "id": "cost",
          "label": "Cost (C)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 50
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "value",
          "label": "Value (V)",
          "formula": "inputs.function / inputs.cost",
          "format": "decimal",
          "unit": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Scenario",
        "Function (F)",
        "Cost (C)",
        "Value (V)"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Current State",
          100,
          50,
          "=100/50"
        ],
        [
          "Enhanced Function",
          150,
          50,
          "=150/50"
        ],
        [
          "Reduced Cost",
          100,
          35,
          "=100/35"
        ],
        [
          "Both Improved",
          150,
          35,
          "=150/35"
        ]
      ]
    }
  ]
}